Each row above lists the grade 8 row in its hands_on in data/progressions/computer-science.csv, and each grade 8 row
lists it in its assumes, except g7-collab-text, whose link is the row change both frames propose. MS-SOC-CE-44 (g8-career-sketch) was owned in grade 6 (g6-careers-ct), but the row assumes
only g7-automation-work, its year-before use.

### Handed on to Grade 9 computer science and beyond

| This course hands on | Unit here | Row that picks it up | What it does with it |
|---|---|---|---|
| g8-network-failure: redraw a map after a failure and add a backup link | 1 | g9-network-sketch | Read a school network diagram and trace one request through it |
| g8-cyber-attacks: common attacks matched to the triangle side and a prevention | 1 | g9-security-measures | Compare security measures and their cost to users |
| g8-choose-a-system: choose a system against another group's requirements, justified line by line | 1 | g9-operating-systems; g9-device-limits | The operating system as a manager layer; a device tested against a task |
| g8-design-for-all: a team's design change for different users' needs, tested | 1 | g11-infrastructure-impact | How computing infrastructure affects access |
| g8-text-project: a designed, built, traced text project with variables, a list and a procedure | 2 | g9-structures-program; g9-design-with-structures; g9-optimize-procedures; g9-modular | Lists and key-value records, structures chosen for a design, procedures with parameters, modules |
| g8-attribution: when credit and permission are needed, and a credit line in code | 2 | g10-apis-docs | Credit a library and its documentation page in a comment |
| g8-refine-for-users: refine a program from classmates' usability and accessibility feedback | 2 | None | The thread ends here in the middle school ids; high school design rows (g10-design-hcd) start from g9 rows |
| g8-relationships: a relationship found with a tool and used to predict or classify | 3 | g9-simulate-data | Generate a simulated dataset to stated parameters |
| g8-investigation-summary: question, method, source, result, limits and biases | 3 | g9-data-dictionary | A data dictionary for a table, each field's type and allowed values |
| g8-biased-decisions: decisions at each data stage that bias a chart or a model | 3 | g9-data-and-people | Large-scale collection, who benefits and who is exposed |
| g8-ml-evaluate: a model's features and limits from its test results and model card | 4 | g9-ai-tour; g9-det-vs-prob | AI algorithm types matched to tasks; deterministic against probabilistic |
| g8-modify-for-bias: a rule changed to remove a harm, retested on the same cases | 4 | g9-algorithm-impacts | A rule-based case audited |
| g8-ai-tool-day: a generated output judged against the problem, on the teacher's one screen | 4 | None | The generated-text thread goes on through g8-evaluate-ai-code |
| g8-evaluate-ai-code: saved generated samples judged for accuracy and usability, first wrong line named | 4 | g10-analyze-code | One saved sample read and traced among the analysis programs |
| g8-emerging-design; g8-emerging-debate: design decisions that change the experience for communities; a local debate with sources | 5 | g9-emerging-differences | An emerging technology set against the established one |
| g8-history-case: a history case reread for what a rule could have done | 5 | g9-computing-history | One technology's trajectory with its social and environmental factors |
| g8-career-sketch: one computing career path, its skills and how automation may change it | 5 | g9-career-interests | A goal, its computing skills and one next step, kept private |

Every hand-on above is answered by that row's assumes in data/progressions/computer-science.csv. Grade 8 ends the
middle school ids: every MS id is owned by grade 8 at the latest (STANDARD.md), and the high school rows start the HS
set with these grade 8 rows as their year-before retrieval.

