"programming","9","g9-structures-program","HS-PRO-VD-16","g8-text-project","g10-analyze-code","text-program; list-diagram; named-box; trace-table","text-program; list-diagram; named-box; trace-table","data structure; list; key-value record; record; index; key; store; access","","Device day. Students write programs that store, find and change data in lists and in key-value records (a roster of animals, a gradebook of made-up scores), tracing each with a list-diagram and a trace-table first. This comes before g9-design-with-structures in the year. Text language only. In-grade order for grade 9: this row before g9-design-with-structures (it writes its design against the structures taught here), and g9-modular after both. Dictionary here is a different thing from the data dictionary of g9-data-dictionary; this row says key-value record."
