## For Cory

- **Scope and attainment rule:** The published PS-05 boundary permits students prohibited from using generative AI to validate teacher-generated output. The current subject rule marks the standard partial whenever a school lacks a live approved tool. Recommend allowing suitably documented, teacher-generated saved outputs to demonstrate full attainment through student validation, while preserving the prohibition on student live-tool use. This changes a settled subject rule, so the fixer must not apply it without Cory�?Ts decision. See [CSTA, PDF page 43](https://csteachers.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/2026-CSTA-PK%E2%80%9312-Computer-Science-Standards.pdf#page=43).

No spending, audience or outside-person decision is needed for the eight frame repairs.

