docs/reviews/frame-computer-science-grade-8-codex-2026-11-25.md:135:### 4. The cybersecurity source map excludes the defenses lesson for the wrong reason
docs/reviews/frame-computer-science-grade-8-codex-2026-11-25.md:152:- Describe lesson 3’s exclusion accurately: its account-hacking scenario and English legal content are outside this adaptation. Retain any needed threat descriptions through Curio Class’s own toy cases.
docs/reviews/frame-computer-science-grade-8-codex-2026-11-25.md:158:### 5. The outgoing network seam omits its grade 10 destination
docs/reviews/frame-computer-science-grade-8-codex-2026-11-25.md:167:`g8-network-failure.hands_on` includes both `g9-network-sketch` and `g10-network-of-networks`. The frame lists only the grade 9 destination. The structural checker identifies this omission.
docs/reviews/frame-computer-science-grade-8-codex-2026-11-25.md:175:Clarify the closing paragraph: grade 9 pickups are year-before retrieval; grade 10 and grade 11 destinations determine readiness from their actual intervening use.
docs/reviews/frame-computer-science-grade-8-codex-2026-11-25.md:177:### 6. Resolved row changes remain described as pending
docs/reviews/frame-computer-science-grade-8-codex-2026-11-25.md:199:### 7. The outside-standard share uses course days instead of teaching days
docs/reviews/frame-computer-science-grade-8-codex-2026-11-25.md:208:The frame divides approximately four list-work days by all 64 course days. C1 specifies teaching days.
docs/reviews/frame-computer-science-grade-8-codex-2026-11-25.md:214:> Approximately four lesson equivalents of list work out of 54 teaching days, about 7.4 percent. The scope and sequence confirms this allocation and counts any other outside-standard teaching within the same limit.
