rest, its skills, its training and how automation may change it, shared at the level of ideas (~MS-SOC-CE-44, used in a new setting, owned in grade 6). Day 62: the year's look-back: each student places one idea from each unit on a one-page map of the five concept areas and writes the question they would take to grade 9. Out: no company or product named in student or teacher copy, no vote that settles a real town question, no policy writing (high school), no technical comparison with the established technology (grade 9's g9-emerging-differences). End-of-unit: the year-end course-level check (day 63) stands for it. Tools: none (all unplugged). Curio Class writes: the two saved transcripts, the route tool case, the credit records case card, the debate packet with two sides and their sources, the career sketch page
